    "body": "When a plugin's HEAD differs from its locked revision but already matches its configured version, the offline update recommended by `:checkhealth vim.pack` reports “Nothing to update” and leaves the mismatch unresolved. A mismatch can also mean the installed revision is intentional and the lockfile is stale, such as after an update with a read-only config directory.\n\nMake both repair choices explicit: restore the lockfile revision with `target = \"lockfile\"`, or keep the installed revision by removing its `rev` entry and restarting to regenerate lockfile data. Add regression tests that follow each recommendation and verify the resulting plugin content and locked revision.\n\nValidation: the package-manager functional test file passes 67 tests, with one network integration test skipped, using the installed Neovim binary at the checkout's commit and the checkout's runtime. StyLua and `git diff --check` pass.\n\nRelated: #38929, #38931.\n\nAI-assisted.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-07T16:12:38Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks, but I think the current wording is both 1) fine and usable; and 2) long enough. For anything more complex there is `vim.pack-examples`, which is a suggested reading for every `vim.pack` user.\r\n\r\nFor the future: there is no testing of a `:checkhealth vim.pack` functionality.",
